    <p><strong>Announcements</strong> from the Administrators appear at the bottom; use <strong>View Announcements</strong> at the top of the page to jump to them. The page updates itself — no need to reload.</p>
</div>

<div class="hc-topic" id="st-times">
    <h3><x-icon name="clock" /> Planned, expected and actual times</h3>
    <p>The time shown next to a group depends on where the day is:</p>
    <div class="hc-panel">
        <div class="hc-legend-row"><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-muted">Planned</span><span>The day has not started. You see the slot the schedule planned.</span></div>
        <div class="hc-legend-row"><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-brand">Expected</span><span>The day is running. Times are re-estimated live from where the room actually is — if presentations run long, later times move later; if they run short, they move earlier.</span></div>
        <div class="hc-legend-row"><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-success">Actual</span><span>Your group already presented (or was deferred). You see when it really happened.</span></div>
        <div class="hc-legend-row"><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-warn">To be scheduled</span><span>Your group still has to present but its day can no longer run (for example, every date has ended). Wait for the Administrator to add a new date — your place is kept.</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hc-note hc-note-warn"><x-icon name="alert-triangle" /><p>Expected times are estimates. <strong>Be at the room well before your expected time</strong> — a group ahead of you may finish early or be deferred.</p></div>
</div>

<div class="hc-topic" id="st-day">
    <h3><x-icon name="calendar-copy" /> On presentation day</h3>
    <ol class="hc-steps">
        <li class="hc-step"><div class="hc-step-marker">1</div><div class="hc-step-body"><div class="hc-step-head"><x-icon name="search" /> Check your room and expected time</div><p class="hc-step-text">Search your group on the schedule page that morning — rooms or times may have changed.</p></div></li>
        <li class="hc-step"><div class="hc-step-marker">2</div><div class="hc-step-body"><div class="hc-step-head"><x-icon name="megaphone" /> Wait to be called</div><p class="hc-step-text">The Lead Panelist calls the next group; your status changes to <span class="hc-badge hc-badge-brand">Called</span>. Go in right away.</p></div></li>
        <li class="hc-step"><div class="hc-step-marker">3</div><div class="hc-step-body"><div class="hc-step-head"><x-icon name="wallet" /> Payment, if required</div><p class="hc-step-text">If the category requires payment, have each receipt's <strong>reference number</strong> ready. The Lead Panelist enters it before you can start. Each reference number can only ever be used once in the system.</p></div></li>
        <li class="hc-step"><div class="hc-step-marker">4</div><div class="hc-step-body"><div class="hc-step-head"><x-icon name="play" /> Present</div><p class="hc-step-text">The timer starts when the Lead presses Start. It turns red and counts extra time if you go over.</p></div></li>
        <li class="hc-step"><div class="hc-step-marker">5</div><div class="hc-step-body"><div class="hc-step-head"><x-icon name="check" /> Completed</div><p class="hc-step-text">After every panelist submits an evaluation, the Lead completes the presentation and your group moves to the Completed list.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
    <h4>If your group is deferred</h4>
    <p>A group can be <span class="hc-badge hc-badge-danger">Deferred</span> — set aside for now. The reasons are: Not Present When Called, Incomplete Group (Member Absent), Not Ready to Present, System / Prototype Not Working, Incomplete Requirements, and Payment Not Verified. A deferred group is <strong>not</strong> removed: it appears in the Deferred list with the reason, and is put back into the queue later (by the Administrator, or automatically at the end of the queue at the end of the day). Talk to the panel or the Administrator if you are unsure.</p>
</div>

<div class="hc-topic" id="st-outcomes">
    <h3><x-icon name="trophy" /> Outcomes and what comes next</h3>
    <p>Each presentation ends with one official outcome — the Lead Panelist's remark:</p>
    <div class="hc-table-wrap">
        <table class="hc-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Outcome</th><th>What it means for your group</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-success">Pass with No Revision</span></td><td>Done. Your grade is final.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-success">Pass with Minor Revision</span></td><td>Done. Make the minor revisions the panel asked for.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-success">Pass with Major Revision</span></td><td>Done. Make the major revisions the panel asked for.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-info">Re-Defense</span></td><td>You present again. The Administrator re-inserts your group; a re-defense always goes <strong>after every other group</strong>, on the last open date, with a new panel.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><span class="hc-badge hc-badge-danger">Failed</span></td><td>Final for this registration. To present again you must <strong>register again</strong> as a new group (the old registration does not block you).</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p>Grades are released by your Administrator. The system does not publish individual grades on the public pages.</p>
</div>
